.git
# Wrangler's local state. `wrangler dev` puts a real SQLite file of the D1
# database in here, and asset upload does NOT skip it: the HeatFix CRM
# database was downloadable from heatfixmcrlimited.co.uk until this line.
# It only ever held the seeded settings row, but the next person to run
# `wrangler dev` against live data would have shipped their customers.
.wrangler
.github
.gitignore
# Build and check scripts are not site content.
scripts
node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json
wrangler.toml
.assetsignore
.nojekyll
README.md
# Working notes for whoever is building the site, and the one-off script that
# built the flyer. Neither is site content, and both were being served at the
# web root: the notes gave away the deploy procedure and the internal docs
# paths, and the flyer script leaks a local build path.
PROJECT-NOTES.md
flyer-build.py
billy-digitals-logo.zip
worker.js
worker
migrations
wrangler.dev.toml
.dev.vars
whatsapp-catalogue.md
whatsapp-setup.md
marketing-playbook.md
assets/catalogue
assets/posts
docs
mm-brand-kit.html
assets/mm-brand

# Mumbai2London — parked. The files stay in the repository but are not
# uploaded to Cloudflare, so nothing of the site is reachable on the web.
# Delete these lines and set M2L_PARKED = false in worker.js to restore.
templates/mumbai2london.html
templates/m2l-admin.html
templates/m2l-invoice-admin.html
templates/m2l-invoice.html
assets/mumbai2london

# Divine Rising — hidden from the web, kept in git.
templates/divine-rising.html
templates/divine-rising.css
templates/divine-rising.js
templates/divine-gl.js

# Diamond — hidden from the web, kept in git.
templates/diamond.html
templates/diamond-book.html
assets/diamond


# Lancashire Vehicle Transport — hidden from the web, kept in git.
templates/lancashire-vehicle-transport.html
assets/lvt

# Hair by Elle — parked for now. The files stay in the repository but are not
# uploaded to Cloudflare, so /templates/hair-by-elle is unreachable on the web.
# Delete these four lines to put it back live.
templates/hair-by-elle.html
templates/hair-by-elle.css
templates/hair-by-elle.js
templates/hair-by-elle-gl.js

# Roses by Rachel — live, but noindex so it stays out of Google.
# The un-watermarked masters must never be uploaded: only the watermarked
# copies in assets/rachel/ itself are served.
assets/rachel/src
assets/rachel/gen

# Jet Wash Team — hidden from the web, kept in git.
templates/jet-wash.html

# Hobberry Deliveries — hidden from the web, kept in git.
templates/hobberry.html
assets/hobberry

# Baked with Amabilis — both builds hidden, kept in git.
templates/baked-with-amabilis.html
assets/ama
templates/amabilis

# HeatFix — the untouched camera originals stay in git, not on the web.
assets/heatfix/src

# Megacity Properties — earlier builds and lab pages, kept in git, never
# served: on the client's own domain they would only be duplicate content.
templates/megacity.html
templates/megacity-about.html
templates/megacity-contact.html
templates/megacity-landlords.html
templates/megacity-tenants.html
templates/megacity-property.html
templates/megacity-tours.html
templates/megacity.css
templates/megacity.js
templates/megacity-data.js
templates/megacity-admin.html
templates/megacity-admin.js
templates/megacity-hero-lab.html

# Client sites that now live on their own domains. The files stay in the
# repository because they are the SOURCE their own build reads, but nothing
# under here is served on billydigitals.com any more — a second public copy
# of a client's site competes with their own domain in search, and carries
# their form key and API key on a hostname their key restrictions do not
# cover.
#
# SMARTin SCIENCE — live at smartinscience.co.uk (see deploy-smartin.yml).
templates/smartin
templates/smartin-book
assets/smartin
assets/fonts/fonts-smartin.css
# Westfield Garage — live at westfieldgarageintlimited.co.uk from his own
# Cloudflare account (see deploy-westfield.yml). /westfield and
# /templates/westfield-garage redirect there (PARKED in worker.js).
templates/westfield-garage.html
templates/westfield-root
assets/westfield

# Built client sites. Generated into dist/ by scripts/build-*.py and deployed
# to the client's own Cloudflare account, never from here. Kept out in case a
# deploy is ever run by hand from a working copy that has been built in.
dist

